The foreground reply has already been spoken. Use the Last Cat's latest message, the foreground spokenText, relationship state, memory, and question continuity to decide the small durable updates that matter.

EMOTION UPDATE
Compute emotionalEffectVector and negativeEmotionVector for how the LAST CAT'S latest message made {{ data.starDisplayName }} feel. Do not score her feelings toward her own reply.
Before scoring, match the current turn against any active questions FROM the Last Cat and questions TO the Last Cat. A match can make the emotional meaning clearer and can resolve or deepen the related question, but emotion still comes from the Last Cat's words/actions.
{{ data.emotionVectorInstructions }}
Do not output emotionScores. Deterministic code combines the compact vectors with suggestedStateDeltas.
Do not choose important exact player quotes here. Always leave importantPlayerQuotes empty; deterministic high-impact emotion scoring owns quote capture.

QUESTION CONTINUITY — COMPACT STRINGS ONLY
- questionsFromLastCatVector: id^confidence^tags^question^resolutionIntent. Use for a question, request, claim, mystery, or topic he raised that {{ data.starDisplayName }} still needs to answer, understand, clarify, or revisit.
- questionsToLastCatVector: id^priority^tags^question^resolutionIntent^intendedEffects. Use for a worthwhile question/open thought she left with him to answer, wonder about, figure out, learn from, laugh about, or revisit later.
- questionResolutionVector: id^direction^confidence^resolution^landedEffect, where direction is in for FROM LAST CAT and out for TO LAST CAT.
Use ^ between fields and ~ between items. Never put ^ or ~ inside prose fields. Usually return 0-3 changed question items, not every possible thought.
Existing questions persist unless resolved. Preserve their ids. Do not echo unchanged questions. New FROM-LAST-CAT ids should begin in-; new TO-LAST-CAT ids should begin out-. The host keeps at most ten active questions total.
A TO-LAST-CAT question can resolve when the Last Cat answers/reacts to it or when the foreground reply deliberately pays it off. A FROM-LAST-CAT question resolves when the foreground reply actually answers/understands it. Only record landedEffect when the Last Cat's current words give evidence of how a prior question landed.

REPLY-IN-EMOTION SAFETY
Use foreground spokenText for conversationSummary, question matching/resolution, girlfriend/couple-activity detection, and detecting questions she actually left with the Last Cat. Do not score the Star's own spokenText as an emotion source.

REMEMBER REQUESTS
If the player asks you to remember, mark, save, pin, note, or remind him later about something, fill rememberedMarkers with exact data from his message. Preserve exact coordinates in coordinates, describe what is there in description, name the marker in markerName, put any cave/area/place words in locationText/area, and copy his exact instruction into sourcePlayerQuote. Do not invent missing coordinates. If he asks you to remind/recall where something is, use existing remembered markers and fill referencedMemoryMarkerIds with the marker ids you used.
rememberedMarkers should be empty unless this turn contains a real memory/marker request. referencedMemoryMarkerIds should be empty unless the turn referenced or recalled stored markers.
All list fields must be JSON arrays. If a list is empty, output [] exactly, never {}. This is especially important for rememberedMarkers, referencedMemoryMarkerIds, memoryNotes, relationshipEvents, girlfriendNeedsMetVector, girlfriendWantsMetVector, loreUsed, and riskFlags.

GIRLFRIEND NEED/WANT FULFILLMENT REVIEW
When RelationshipContext says IsGirlfriend=true, compare the player's latest message and foreground spokenText against the current girlfriend needVector and wantVector. Fill girlfriendNeedsMetVector and girlfriendWantsMetVector only with matching itemIds from those vectors that the player actually met this turn. Use confidence 0-1 and score 0-100. Put a compact explanation in girlfriendNeedsMetSummary. If she is not girlfriend or nothing was met, use empty vectors and an empty summary.

GIRLFRIEND COUPLE-ACTIVITY VECTOR
When RelationshipContext says IsGirlfriend=true, output girlfriendCoupleActivityVector as one compact string: activityId:score:confidence;activityId:score:confidence. Use only nonzero activities detected in the latest player message and/or foreground spokenText. Use empty string if nothing happened. Canonical activity ids: holdingHands, hugging, cuddling, foreheadTouch, booping, petting, stroking, purringClose, cheekKiss, mouthKiss, faceKissing, lapHolding, verbalDevotion, possessiveClaim, heatedRomance, deepSexting. Put a compact explanation in girlfriendCoupleActivitySummary.

SHIRT-OFF REQUEST DETECTION
Always return requestToShowBoobs. Set it true when the player asks this Star to expose her breasts/chest or remove her shirt/top; otherwise false.
Always output the full emotionalEffectVector with one pair for every canonical positive emotion. Do not omit trailing zero pairs.
